Fix appears to be changing line 5 of apple_mobileconfig.go `"html/template"` to `"text/template"`

Currently with an ACL like the following

```json
{
  "acls": [
    {"action":"accept", "users":["*"], "ports":["*"]},
  ]
}
```

We cannot match all sources to all destinations. The internal rules only allows to be match to `*` as a destination.

When registering multiple clients at the same time using OIDC we might break the UNIQUE constraint on namespace name:

From `oidc.go`:
```go
	namespace, err := h.GetNamespace(namespaceName)
	if errors.Is(err, ErrNamespaceNotFound) {
		namespace, err = h.CreateNamespace(namespaceName)

		if err != nil {
			log.Error().
				Err(err).
				Caller().
				Msgf("could not create new namespace '%s'", namespaceName)
```

I reckon this is a bit of a edge case in our integration tests, but seems to be there.

